      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you work on Woolton's listed buildings?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Woolton Conservation Area covers a large part of the village. Many properties on Beaconsfield Road, Quarry Street and Church Road are listed or in the conservation area. We plan installations around original features. For listed buildings we provide paperwork suitable for listed building consent applications." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can you find a hidden leak without opening walls?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, in most cases. We carry thermal imaging equipment that detects temperature differences behind walls and under floors. This pinpoints the source of a hidden leak before any plasterwork is opened. We always try non-invasive leak location first. Call 0151 558 0334." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you cover larger detached homes with multi-zone heating?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The detached homes on Hillside Drive, Baroncroft Road and the wider Woolton area often have two or three heating zones, unvented mains pressure cylinders feeding multiple bathrooms, and premium fixtures. We're G3 qualified for unvented work and familiar with Hansgrohe, Grohe, Villeroy & Boch and other premium brands." } },
