    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">WOOLTON LOCAL KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>Why Woolton Needs a Plumber Who Knows L25</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Woolton is Liverpool's most affluent suburb. The L25 average property price sits around £401,000. Beaconsfield Road plots have changed hands at £10,000-plus per square foot. The top end runs £1.5 million to £2.4 million.</p>

        <p>That matters when something leaks. A burst pipe in a detached Quarry Street home can damage original cornicing, period floorboards and high-end finishes within minutes. The cost of restoration is high. Speed and accurate diagnosis save real money.</p>

        <p>Woolton Conservation Area also restricts what you can do externally. New flues, satellite dishes, condensate runs and any visible alterations to listed properties need planning consent. We've worked in the conservation area for years. We plan installations to avoid problems with the council.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>Most Woolton properties are owner-occupied. People here tend to stay. The plumbing has been extended and modified many times across each property's life. Original pipework runs alongside 1970s additions and modern combi boiler retrofits.</p>

        <p>Finding a leak in a 5-bed detached with three bathrooms and a long history of plumbing changes takes experience. Water shows up at one point. It often starts somewhere else entirely. We carry thermal imaging and acoustic leak detection to trace the source before opening any plasterwork.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
