        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Woolton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£80 an hour weekdays 9am to 5pm. £120 an hour weekends 9am to 1pm. £150 an hour out of hours, nights and bank holidays. 1 hour minimum on every call-out. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost £80 to £350 total. Written quote before work starts. No separate call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Woolton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>30 minute response guaranteed across Woolton L25. We dispatch from Kirkby. Typical arrival is 25 to 30 minutes via the M62 and M57. A real person answers the phone any time of day or night.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LISTED</span>&nbsp; Do you work on Woolton's listed buildings?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Woolton Conservation Area covers a large part of the village. Many properties on Beaconsfield Road, Quarry Street and Church Road are listed or in the conservation area. We plan installations around original features. For listed buildings we provide paperwork suitable for listed building consent applications.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LEAKS</span>&nbsp; Can you find a hidden leak without opening walls?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes, in most cases. We carry thermal imaging equipment that detects temperature differences behind walls and under floors. This pinpoints the source of a hidden leak before any plasterwork is opened. We always try non-invasive leak location first. Call 0151 558 0334 for a same-day assessment.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">DETACHED</span>&nbsp; Do you cover larger detached homes with multi-zone heating?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The detached homes on Hillside Drive, Baroncroft Road and the wider Woolton area often have two or three heating zones, unvented mains pressure cylinders feeding multiple bathrooms, and premium fixtures. We're G3 qualified for unvented work and familiar with Hansgrohe, Grohe, Villeroy & Boch and other premium brands.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">RETIREMENT</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Reynolds Court and other retirement properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Reynolds Court on Vale Road and the wider retirement housing stock in Woolton are familiar work. We coordinate with managing agents where access is needed to communal areas. We explain faults clearly without jargon and confirm pricing up front before any work begins.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All our engineers are Gas Safe registered. It's illegal to carry out gas work without this qualification. Verify our registration at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We provide gas safety certificates for all gas work carried out.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
